 to handle 6-bit support given typical 4/8-bit tooling defaults. Explicitly flag anything you cannot verify from the repository alone.\\n\\nDo not produce the full final design yet — this turn is only about inspection, approach, and assumptions.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"How well does QuaRot generalize to non-LLAMA models like Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct? Specifically, how do RTN and GPTQ compare in perplexity and zero-shot accuracy across 4-bit, 6-bit, and 8-bit quantization?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 224, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [\"neurips2024/94328/9:setup_1\", \"neurips2024/94328/9:setup_3\", \"neurips2024/94328/9:setup_4\", \"neurips2024/94328/9:setup_6\", \"neurips2024/94328/9:setup_8\", \"neurips2024/94328/9:setup_11\"], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
